  "notes": "Drawn from two A220-300s in early 2026 (N256BZ left, N237BZ right). Breeze launched in 2021 with a white fuselage and navy tail; this all-blue scheme replaced it later (its year isn't confirmed here, so 'from' is left out), and some aircraft may still wear the white one. The navy section's pale diagonals are simplified. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on N256BZ (near side-on) and N237BZ: the title sits under the windows (cap height y -0.175 to 0.1, x 0.177 to 0.339; it had been drawn reaching over them), lowercase 0.75 of the B; the tick crosses the windows over the 'ee' (centred y 0.2, 0.3 tall); the navy's front edge is a convex curve, now smooth. 'flybreeze.com' added: small, under the wing's trailing edge, mostly hidden by the flaps on the left photo and seen whole on the right (x about 0.59 to 0.67 once the right photo's perspective is allowed for; low).",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximate standard (a few colors from memory)."
